results.evidence:
In `InviteModal.tsx`, the user's own email is detected and flags the row with error styling and an inline message:
```tsx
const isOwnEmail = !!email && email.trim().toLowerCase() === user?.email?.trim().toLowerCase()
const emailError = isOwnEmail
    ? "You can't invite yourself."
...
<LemonInput className={`error-on-blur${!invitesToSend[index]?.isValid || emailError ? ' errored' : ''}`} ... />
{emailError && (
    <div className="mt-1 text-xs text-danger" role="alert">
        {emailError}
    </div>
)}
```

The member list is not fetched when opening the invite form; instead, `checkInviteEmail` queries a newly introduced backend endpoint per email:
```tsx
checkInviteEmail: async ({ email }) => {
    try {
        const organizationId = organizationLogic.values.currentOrganizationId
        const result = await api.get(
            `api/organizations/${organizationId}/invites/check_email/?email=${encodeURIComponent(email)}`
        )
```
